  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#history-pushstate\n\nin the definition of pushState/replaceState methods, the step stating:\n\n> Compare the resulting URL record to the result of applying the URL parser algorithm to the document's address. If any component of these two URLs differ other than the path, query, and fragment components, then throw a SecurityError exception and abort these steps.\n\nSince document's address is defined to be a URL record in the DOM spec, it seems redundant to reparse it.\n\nAlso, in the same method definition, the step stating:\n\n> Let new URL be the resulting absolute URL.\n\nshould be rephrased as:\n\n> Let new URL be the resulting URL record.\n\n( But it is uncertain for me that, URL of entrys in the session history are defined to be a URL record or a URL string )\n",
